<p>A guinea pig that stops eating is always an emergency, not a "wait and see" situation. Guinea pigs have a digestive system that relies on a constant stream of fibre moving through it, and even a few hours without food can let gut motility slow down and spiral into a dangerous condition called <strong>GI stasis</strong>. This guide explains the most common causes of appetite loss in guinea pigs, the early warning signs of GI stasis, and what to do right now if your guinea pig has gone quiet at the food bowl.</p>

